schema: "0.3"
id: echo-of-manifestation-map-bleached-asylum
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  text: >
    Top-down dungeon map of the Bleached Asylum — Zone 3 of Echo of Manifestation, a survival horror
    roguelite. Dark fantasy game design document style, bird's-eye architectural floor plan.

    The map shows a sterile institutional complex with these rooms connected by white-walled shadow
    corridors that feature LOOPING HALLWAY connections (marked with circular arrows indicating paths
    that repeat unless the player finds the correct sequence):

    ENTRY (east): A decontamination antechamber from Zone 2's threshold corridor. Flickering
    fluorescent light icon. Small resonance shrine on a gurney.

    DAYROOM WARD — COMBAT (center): 16m x 14m communal patient dayroom. Overturned tables and
    bolted-down furniture drawn as geometric shapes. Faded murals on walls depicted as distorted
    face outlines. Chalk residue zones marked with textured floor fill. Two essence nodes: behind
    collapsed vending machine, inside a mural alcove. Four shadow nodes: inside ceiling light
    fixtures, under bolted tables, behind murals, inside a locker.

    PHARMACY GRID — PUZZLE (south): 12m x 8m medication dispensary. Rows of labeled cabinets drawn
    as wall-mounted grids. Patient file fragments marked as small document icons. One essence node
    inside the correct compound cabinet. Two shadow nodes behind wrong-compound cabinets. Toxic gas
    hazard zones marked with green cloud symbols. Sound trigger icons (speaker symbols) near
    cabinet interaction points.

    ELECTROTHERAPY CHAMBER — LOOT (north): 10m x 12m abandoned shock therapy room. Still-humming
    generator drawn as a large mechanical unit. Electrodes dangling from ceiling marked as danger
    hazard lines. Locked medicine cabinet on far wall. Three essence nodes: medicine cabinet, inside
    generator housing, under treatment chair. One shadow node attached to a live electrode cluster.
    A TIME DILATION POCKET behind the generator, accessible only after disabling it via power switch.

    FORGOTTEN BASEMENT WARD — SECRET (accessible via hidden elevator shaft from Dayroom Ward):
    14m x 10m sealed-off basement ward drawn with dashed border. Padded cells lining the corridor
    drawn with cushion-textured walls. Scratch marks on cell interiors. Resonance anomaly at center
    room shown as a swirling distortion symbol. Two essence nodes: most damaged cell, center anomaly.
    Three shadow nodes: inside padded cells, behind peeling wallpaper. Perception distortion hazard
    zone marked with inverted minimap icon. Hidden shop NPC icon at anomaly location.

    DIRECTOR'S OPERATING THEATER — BOSS (west): 18m x 16m surgical theater. Operating table at arena
    center. Observation galleries on three sides drawn as elevated platforms with railings. Surgical
    tools along walls marked as projectile hazard icons. Three essence nodes: observation gallery left,
    gallery right, behind surgical tool rack. Five shadow nodes: inside overhead lights, under table,
    among tools, in drainage grates, behind gallery glass. A TIME DILATION POCKET behind observation
    gallery accessible in boss phase 2. Boss marker: "RESONANT CHOIR" with a multi-voice speaker
    array icon. Hallway loop connections shown with curved arrows linking this room back to the
    Dayroom Ward (player can get lost in looping corridors if they don't follow sound cues).

    The looping hallway mechanic is the signature feature of this zone — multiple corridors between
    rooms have dual connections shown with circular path indicators. Sound cue markers (musical note
    icons) indicate the correct path — silence means safe passage.

    Map legend: Amber diamond = Essence Node, Purple circle = Shadow Node, Golden bubble = Time
    Dilation Pocket, Dashed border = Secret Room, Skull icon = Boss, Curved arrow = Looping Hallway,
    Speaker icon = Sound Trigger, Green cloud = Toxic Gas.

    Style: Architectural blueprint on off-white/cream background with clinical green grid lines.
    Room walls in stark white with rust stain accents at junctions. Fluorescent flicker effect
    rendered as uneven lighting in corridor connections. Shadows too sharp — harsh edge shadows
    within rooms. Professional game design document aesthetic with institutional coldness.
  negative: "bright colors, cartoon, anime, 3D rendered, photorealistic, warm tones, cheerful, colorful, messy hand-drawn, low detail, gothic"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1536
    aspect_ratio: "1:1"

tags: [map, zone-3, bleached-asylum, top-down, dungeon-map, game-design-document, dark-fantasy, institutional]
